On 2026-09-23 the owner decided ProjectMapper should be finished and publicly released.
v1.0.0 released on GitHub (tag v1.0.0; release "ProjectMapper 1.0.0", wheel+sdist; NOT on PyPI).
Acceptance report docs/acceptance/v1.0.0.md. 335 tests on 3.10/3.13/3.14.

Tranche 9 (CLI + MCP): entry approved 2026-09-26. Owner decisions: F1 `mcp` SDK as optional extra;
F2 agents MAY transform files (safely) with root confinement, forced backups, fingerprints;
F3 human-in-the-loop approval popup in the adapter process (default deny, timeout deny, exact diff);
F5 result limits are user settings (per-user settings.json + desktop Settings window);
F6 names projectmapper-cli/-mcp, release 1.1.0.

Why: the owner believes the project "should exist"; the two-way project<->LLM bridge with human approval is the differentiator.
How to apply: follow tranche-workflow and gui-probe-safety; never push or publish without explicit approval; verify this status against git before relying on it.
